{"title":"2020 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1c","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Using_Slope_of_Line)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Using Slope of Line)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Using_Point_D)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Using Point D)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Finding_Slope_of_Library_Line)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Finding Slope of Library Line)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2020 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Annie (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />), Bogdan (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />), Cao (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />), Daniel (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />), and Emily (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />) are running for student government positions. Their campaign posters are printed by different printing companies. The graph below plots each student’s total price of their first batch of posters versus the number of posters in their first batch.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>(put graph on problem 1 page)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In Daniel's second batch, he needs to print <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> posters. He can pay <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/1/111a2d40e75492a05323f2a6201015e2cceea269.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$60.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" /> to print these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> posters at his local library. To spend less money on the second batch, should Daniel print these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> posters at the library, or should he continue to pay the same price per poster using the company that printed his first batch?\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Using_Slope_of_Line.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Using_Slope_of_Line)\">Solution 1 (Using Slope of Line)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Using Slope of Line)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1a\" title=\"2020 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1a\">problem 1a</a>, Daniel pays <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/3/c030e1eabde01498527b3c53e08763522c0c7da2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$1.60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> per poster with the first company that produced his first batch.\n</p><p>Thus, if Daniel went with that same company, he would have paid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/e/5ae8a62e7c0f0a529009a1a6c937594a7ebe4171.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$1.60 \\times 40 = \\$64.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"158\" height=\"17\" /> in total. Since this costs more than printing the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> posters at the library, Daniel should print the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> posters at the library.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Using_Point_D.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Using_Point_D)\">Solution 2 (Using Point D)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Using Point D)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the graph, we see that point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/2/a32d7a56610b4e6d5aa683acac1c83d8bdda051a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(10, \\$16)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"70\" height=\"20\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> posters is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> posters repeated <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times, staying with the first company that produced his first batch would have cost <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/25564f4e898ba90781f8fb9083d683c962ccd02c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$16.00 \\times 4 = \\$64.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"158\" height=\"17\" /> in ttoal.\n</p><p>Since this costs more than printing the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> posters at the library, Daniel should print the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> posters at the library.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Finding_Slope_of_Library_Line.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Finding_Slope_of_Library_Line)\">Solution 3 (Finding Slope of Library Line)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Finding Slope of Library Line)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since Daniel is printing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> posters and the cost is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/1/111a2d40e75492a05323f2a6201015e2cceea269.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$60.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" /> at the library, he must pay <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3bba3dfa9e362a81f63497867c2a5ff22f4fb49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\$60.00}{40} = \\$1.50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"122\" height=\"40\" /> per poster at the library.\n</p><p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1a\" title=\"2020 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1a\">problem 1a</a>, Daniel pays <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/3/c030e1eabde01498527b3c53e08763522c0c7da2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$1.60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> per poster with the first company that produced his first batch. This is more than the cost per poster at the library, so Daniel should print the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> posters at the library.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018012728\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.085 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 133/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1259/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4568/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.745      1 2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1\n100.00%   13.745      1 -total\n 38.49%    5.290      1 Template:Image_needed\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36891:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018012728 and revision id 285643. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}